   "definition": "",
   "video_id": "849669848"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Differentiating other functions"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I differentiate common functions?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- These are the common results\n\n  - $\\frac{d}{dx}(x^{n})=nx^{n-1}$\n  - $\\frac{d}{dx}(e^{x})=e^{x}$\n  - $\\frac{d}{dx}(a^{x})=a^{x}\\mathrm{ln}a$ for $a>0$\n  - $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\mathrm{ln}x)=\\frac{1}{x}$\n  - $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\mathrm{sin}x)=\\mathrm{cos}x$\n  - $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\mathrm{cos}x)=-\\mathrm{sin}x$\n  - $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\mathrm{tan}x)=\\mathrm{sec}^{2}x$\n  - $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\mathrm{cot}x)=-\\mathrm{cos} \\mathrm{ec}^{2}x$\n  - $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\mathrm{sec}x)=\\mathrm{sec}x\\mathrm{tan}x$\n  - $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\mathrm{cos} \\mathrm{ec}x)=-\\mathrm{cos} \\mathrm{ec}x\\mathrm{cot}x$"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "How do I differentiate e<sup>kx</sup>, a<sup>x</sup>, ln(kx) and a<sup>kx</sup>?"
